<h1>Destruction</h1>
<p>Destruction lets authored objects split into physical groups when bonds fail. This page covers the component recipe, spatial impacts and part damage, state queries, checkpoints, and debris cleanup.</p>

<h2>What destruction is</h2>
<p>An ordinary scene or prefab can carry a compact fracture recipe. Cooking prepares its geometry; at runtime, accepted impacts and part damage queue changes to the physical assembly. Gameplay chooses when to issue those calls and checks <code>state</code> for the committed result.</p>

